From 1676e7172a3a73cec18ed22c30e23d4da8889237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 00:14:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): overlap tie-break only + post-budget title fence
 (W1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Final W1 review round (Codex P2s):
- routeSkill: description-overlap is now a TIE-BREAKER among curated hits only;
  a prompt with no INTENT_RULES hit returns unknown:true, so a generic non-Forge
  prompt ("please review this commit") no longer routes into a workflow stage.
- prime live-state: the claimed-issue title is no longer fenced inline; the whole
  live-state block is emitted as a section carrying untrustedSource, so the shared
  post-budget fenceUntrustedSections wraps it and the ⟦END UNTRUSTED⟧ terminator
  survives budget truncation (e.g. forge prime --budget 45).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/orientation.js                        | 78 +++++++++++++++++------
 lib/using-forge.js                        | 12 +++-
 test/orientation-prime-live-state.test.js | 75 ++++++++++++----------
 test/using-forge.test.js                  | 12 +++-
 4 files changed, 118 insertions(+), 59 deletions(-)

